"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids March to April and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years. In 2025 on the middle, March to April came in at 28% of normal and November to December at 47%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 39% and June to July at 78% on the county&rsquo;s middle value. Grid 10394 had its driest year in 2000 at 61% of normal.</p>"}
